   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,207:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 🔷 UNIT 1: INTRODUCTION TO DATA SCIENCE
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,354:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.1 What is Data Science?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,354:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Data Science
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,357:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is a field that combines statistics, mathematics, programming, and domain knowledge to extract
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,358:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: meaningful insights from data.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,358:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: In simple words:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,359:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  You have raw data → you clean it → analyse it → build models → make predictions or decisions.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,368:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Key Components:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,369:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,370:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Mathematics 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,371:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,371:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Statistics
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,372:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — Probability, distributions, hypothesis testing.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,373:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,373:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Programming
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,374:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — Python, R, SQL for data manipulation.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,375:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,376:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Domain Knowledge
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,376:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — Understanding the business problem (healthcare, finance, etc).
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,377:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,378:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Machine Learning
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,378:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — Algorithms that learn from data.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,379:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,380:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Visualization
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,380:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — Communicating findings through charts and graphs.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,382:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.2 What is Big Data?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,382:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Big Data
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,383:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  = Datasets that are so large, fast, and complex that traditional tools (like Excel or MySQL) can
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,384:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,385:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t handle
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,385:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: them.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,386:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Think of it this way:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,390:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Excel can handle thousands of rows. But what if you have 10 billion rows of GPS data from
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,390:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Uber drivers streaming in every second? That
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,391:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,392:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s Big Data.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,392:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The 5 V
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,393:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,393:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s of Big Data
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,394:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | V | What it means | Real Example | Why it matters |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,395:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,396:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,396:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,397:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,397:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Volume
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,402:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  | Massive amount of data |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,403:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Facebook: 4+ petabytes/day (1 PB = 10 lakh GB) | Need distributed storage (Hadoop, cloud) |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,403:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,404:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,405:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Velocity
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,408:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  | Speed of
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,409:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: data generation | Stock market: millisecond updates | Need real-time processing (Kafka, Spark) |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,410:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,411:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,411:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Variety
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,416:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  | Different
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,417:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: types of data | Text + images + videos + GPS + audio | Need tools that handle all formats |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,417:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,418:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,419:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Veracity
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,422:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  | Quality and
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,423:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: trustworthiness | Twitter bots posting fake news | Need data validation and cleaning |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,424:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,425:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,425:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Value
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,430:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  | Usefulness after
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,431:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: processing | Netflix recommendations → saves $1B/year | Raw data is useless; insights are valuable |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,432:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tools for Big Data:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,433:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,433:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Storage:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,434:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Hadoop HDFS, Amazon S3, Google Cloud Storage
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,435:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,436:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Processing:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,436:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Apache Spark, MapReduce
   DEBUG: 2026-04-04 01:02:32,437:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
